# Project Structure

**GOAL**: Create a standardized, AI-optimized project structure that enables effective knowledge management, consistent development workflows, and seamless AI assistance across any Cursor project.

## Required Project Structure

**Use this exact structure for every new Cursor project:**

```
project-root/
├── .cursor/
│   ├── rules/             # Project-specific AI rules
│   └── project.md         # AI agent context (REQUIRED)
├── .foam/                 # Knowledge workspace
│   └── templates/         # Daily note templates
├── .github/               # Automation & templates
│   ├── workflows/         # CI/CD pipelines
│   ├── ISSUE_TEMPLATE/    # Issue templates
│   └── pull_request_template.md
├── README.md              # Project overview (REQUIRED)
├── memories/              # AI knowledge base (REQUIRED)
│   ├── knowledge/         # Facts, learnings, documentation
│   ├── plans/             # Goals, roadmaps, strategies
│   ├── decisions/         # ADRs (Architectural Decision Records)
│   ├── tasks/             # Task management, todos
│   ├── conversations/     # AI conversation exports (from chi)
│   ├── notes/             # Daily notes, observations
│   └── lessons-learned/   # What worked, what didn't, retrospectives
└── [project-specific]/    # Your actual project code
    ├── src/               # Source code (if applicable)
    ├── docs/              # Project documentation
    └── [other]/           # Project-specific directories
```

## Step-by-Step Project Setup

**Follow this exact sequence for new projects:**

### 1. Create Core Structure

```bash
mkdir -p .cursor/rules .foam/templates .github/{workflows,ISSUE_TEMPLATE} memories/{knowledge,plans,decisions,tasks,conversations,notes,lessons-learned}
```

### 2. Initialize Project Context

**Create `.cursor/project.md` with this template:**

```markdown
---
title: "[Project Name]"
description: "Brief project description"
status: "active"
created: "[date]"
---

# [Project Name] - AI Context

## Project Overview

- **Purpose**: What this project accomplishes
- **Type**: Application, library, documentation, etc.
- **Audience**: Who uses this project

## Core Objectives

1. **Primary Goal**: Main deliverable
2. **Secondary Goals**: Supporting objectives
3. **Success Metrics**: How you measure success

## Technical Context

- **Stack**: Technologies, frameworks, languages
- **Architecture**: System design, patterns
- **Constraints**: Performance, security, compatibility requirements

## Development Workflow

- **AI Integration**: How AI assists development
- **Memory Routing**: Where different types of content go
- **Review Process**: Code review, testing, deployment

## Current Status

- **Phase**: Planning, development, testing, production
- **Next Steps**: Immediate priorities
- **Blockers**: Current obstacles
- **Timeline**: Key milestones
```

### 3. Set Up Memory System

**Create these essential memory files:**

- `memories/knowledge/project-overview.md` - Core project facts
- `memories/plans/roadmap.md` - Development roadmap
- `memories/decisions/README.md` - ADR template

### 4. Configure GitHub Integration

**Add these files:**

- `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/bug_report.md`
- `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/feature_request.md`
- `.github/pull_request_template.md`

## Memory System Rules

**Route content to the correct memory folder:**

| Content Type           | Destination                 | Example                      |
| ---------------------- | --------------------------- | ---------------------------- |
| Facts, learnings       | `memories/knowledge/`       | "React hooks best practices" |
| Goals, roadmaps        | `memories/plans/`           | "Q1 2024 roadmap"            |
| Architecture decisions | `memories/decisions/`       | "ADR-001: Database choice"   |
| Tasks, todos           | `memories/tasks/`           | "Implement user auth"        |
| AI conversations       | `memories/conversations/`   | "Design discussion with AI"  |
| Daily notes            | `memories/notes/`           | "2024-01-15 progress"        |
| Lessons learned        | `memories/lessons-learned/` | "What worked in sprint 1"    |

**REQUIRED**: Include YAML frontmatter in ALL markdown files:

```yaml
---
title: "File Title"
description: "Brief description"
created: "2024-01-15"
tags: ["tag1", "tag2"]
---
```

## Cursor Rules Integration

**Project-specific rules go in `.cursor/rules/`:**

- Reference global rules from main cursor system
- Add project-specific context only when needed
- Always include prompt improvement and memory system rules
- Keep rules focused and actionable

## File Organization Standards

**Naming Conventions:**

- Use kebab-case for files: `user-authentication.md`
- Use descriptive names: `database-schema-v2.md`
- Include dates for time-sensitive content: `2024-01-15-daily-notes.md`

**Content Standards:**

- Start every file with YAML frontmatter
- Use clear headings and structure
- Include context and examples
- Link related files and resources

## AI Integration Workflow

**Daily Development Process:**

1. **Start**: Check `memories/plans/` for current priorities
2. **Work**: Use AI assistance with project context
3. **Document**: Route learnings to appropriate memory folders
4. **Review**: Export important conversations to `memories/conversations/`
5. **Plan**: Update `memories/plans/` with progress and next steps

**REMEMBER**: This structure enables AI agents to understand your project context, access relevant knowledge, and provide better assistance. Always maintain the memory system and keep project context current.
